\description{
The core function: the rows of one dataset at one detail level, as a
tibble typed from the dataset's schema, with place names beside their
codes.

\strong{It returns every category and group the filters don't exclude.}
Nothing is pinned by default: no single demographic group, no single
subject. A call with only a dataset name returns the whole dataset at
its default detail level.
}
\section{Filters}{

Give filters as named arguments in \code{...}; each value is a vector.
Values within one filter are OR'd; different filters are AND'd.
Accepted names:
\itemize{
\item any categorical column: \code{subject = "mathematics"},
\code{demographic = c("all", "black")};
\item geography codes: \code{district_code}, \code{school_code}, \code{county_fips},
\code{tract_geoid}, \code{block_group_geoid};
\item \code{school_id}: schools as \code{"DISTRICT-SCHOOL"} codes
(\code{school_id = c("761-0199", "660-0104")}), the form \code{\link[=gcd_locate]{gcd_locate()}}
returns (a school code alone is not unique across districts);
\item lookup-table attributes: \code{district_type = "state_charter"},
\code{school_level = "high"}, \code{locale = "rural"},
\code{demographic_category = "race"};
\item metric bounds: \code{graduation_rate_min = 0.9}, \code{num_cohort_max = 50}
(inclusive, in stored units).
}

\code{NA} in a filter selects rows where a nullable column is empty;
logicals become \code{true} / \code{false}. The API validates every filter and
its errors name what went wrong; \code{\link[=gcd_describe]{gcd_describe()}} lists each dataset's
filters and their values.
}

\section{Labels}{

With \code{labels = TRUE} (the default) the rows carry the API's joined name
columns, each right after its code: \code{district_name},
\code{district_census_id} and \code{district_type} after \code{district_code};
\code{school_name} after \code{school_code}; \code{county_name}, \code{tract_name} and
\code{block_group_name} after their codes; \code{demographic_label} and
\code{demographic_category} after \code{demographic}. Codes are always kept:
school names repeat across districts, names change over time, and joins
run on codes.
\itemize{
\item Categorical values (\code{subject}, \code{grade_cluster}) are readable
snake_case codes already; there are no separate labels for them.
\item \code{demographic_category} (race, gender, economic_status, ...) is a
grouping that arrives with the labels; filtering by it works either
way.
\item Other lookup-table attributes (school addresses, locale, coordinates)
are not joined; get them from \code{\link[=gcd_dimension]{gcd_dimension()}} and join.
}

\code{labels = FALSE} asks for the dataset's own columns only, for large
pulls. Either way, code columns that would be empty on every row (a
district row's \code{school_code}, a state row's geography codes) are left
out, so both settings give the same shape.
}

\section{Missing values and totals}{

\code{NA} in a metric usually means the value was \strong{suppressed} to protect
privacy (small counts), \strong{not zero}; the schema's \code{null_semantics} says
which (\code{\link[=gcd_describe]{gcd_describe()}}). Because nothing is pinned, results hold the
\code{all} totals beside the subgroups: never add a total to its subgroups.
The API's advisories say so when they apply, and print once per call as
messages (\code{quiet = TRUE} or \code{options(gcd.quiet = TRUE)} silences them;
they stay in \code{gcd_meta(x)$advisories}).

Rates must be pooled from their counts, never averaged:
\code{sum(num_graduates) / sum(num_cohort)}, not \code{mean(graduation_rate)}.
\code{\link[=gcd_columns]{gcd_columns()}} shows each metric's numerator and denominator.
}

\section{Large downloads and the disk cache}{

Up to 10,000 rows come back as one JSON page. A larger result is
downloaded in full as CSV in one response (with a progress bar); the
metadata and advisories then come from the first JSON page and describe
its first 10,000 rows.

With \code{cache = TRUE} (or \code{options(gcd.cache = TRUE)}), responses are kept
in \code{tools::R_user_dir("georgiacivicdata", "cache")} with their \code{ETag}.
Repeating a request asks the server whether the data changed: an
unchanged answer reuses the saved copy without downloading, and a new
data release downloads afresh. A response the server marks fresh (for
five minutes) is reused without asking. Clear it with
\code{\link[=gcd_cache_clear]{gcd_cache_clear()}}.
}

\section{Data license}{

The data is CC BY 4.0: credit Georgia Civic Data and the original
source, as \code{\link[=gcd_citation]{gcd_citation()}} writes.
}

